# Prefer padding over margin

Avoid `margin` / Tailwind `m-*`, `mx-*`, `my-*`, `mt-*`, `mb-*`, `ml-*`, `mr-*` for layout spacing. Prefer **`padding`** (`p-*`, `px-*`, `py-*`, …) and, in flex/grid, **`gap`**.

Vertical margins collapse in surprising ways (siblings, parent/child, same-direction). Padding does not. Details: [The Rules of Margin Collapse](https://www.joshwcomeau.com/css/rules-of-margin-collapse/) (Josh Comeau).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — margins collapse between siblings / into parents
<div className="mt-4 mb-4">…</div>
<p className="my-6">…</p>

// ✅ GOOD — padding on the container (or gap in flex/grid)
<section className="flex flex-col gap-4 p-4">…</section>
<div className="px-4 py-2">…</div>
```

Exceptions (rare):

- Flex/grid utilities that are not “spacing between blocks”: `mx-auto`, `ml-auto` / `ms-auto`, `mt-auto`, etc.
- Negative pull hacks (`-ms-1`) and absolute offsets better expressed with `left`/`top`/`calc`
- shadcn/`components/ui` primitives (separators, carousel defaults) unless a local override is clearly safer
- Domain fields named `*_margin` (unrelated to CSS)

Prefer fixing structure / using `gap` before adding margin.
